---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const sections = [
  {
    emoji: '🎯',
    title: 'Pick and practice',
    items: [
      'Choose a challenge together. Let each kid veto one, so both are excited.',
      'Watch the tutorial at half speed first, then learn the dance in small chunks (8 counts at a time).',
      'Practice facing a mirror, then film a rehearsal on your phone and watch it back together.',
      'Pick a challenge that fits both ages. Easy ones can pair a 7th grader and a 4th grader without anyone feeling left behind.',
    ],
  },
  {
    emoji: '📱',
    title: 'Set up the shot',
    items: [
      'Shorts and Reels are vertical (9:16). Hold the phone upright. Use horizontal only for a regular YouTube video.',
      'Put the phone at about waist height, and leave room above heads and below feet so everyone fits in the frame.',
      'Prop the phone on a stack of books or a cheap tripod so it stays still. Tape a mark on the floor for where to stand.',
      'Clean up the background. Use the back camera if you can, since it is usually sharper than the selfie camera.',
    ],
  },
  {
    emoji: '💡',
    title: 'Light and sound',
    items: [
      'Face the light. A window in front of the dancers works better than one behind them.',
      'Avoid dark clothes against a dark wall, and avoid busy patterns that blur on camera.',
      'Play the song from a speaker so the dancers can hear it. Keep the volume steady across takes.',
      'Wear shoes with grip, and clear the floor. Safe and comfortable beats fancy.',
    ],
  },
  {
    emoji: '🎬',
    title: 'Film and edit',
    items: [
      'Start recording a few seconds early and use a 3-2-1 count so every take starts together.',
      'Film several takes. The 3rd or 4th is usually the best one, and the outtakes are fun to keep.',
      'Trim the start and end in a free editor (for example the YouTube Create app or CapCut), then add a short title.',
      'Add the song and challenge name in the description so viewers can find the original.',
    ],
  },
  {
    emoji: '🛡️',
    title: 'Upload safely',
    items: [
      'In YouTube Studio, set the audience for kids correctly for each video. YouTube asks you to choose, and the answer changes how comments and ads work.',
      'Think about turning comments off or holding them for review, especially for videos with children.',
      'Do not show names, school logos or uniforms, the street, or other details that reveal where the kids live or go to school.',
      'Check location settings on the phone, and avoid sharing the video link in public places that identify the kids.',
      'Popular songs are often covered by copyright. Videos may get a claim or be muted. Picking the song from the music library inside YouTube Shorts is usually the safest route, and the YouTube Audio Library has free music.',
      'Ask the kids before posting. If one of them is not happy with the video, do not upload it.',
    ],
  },
];

const checklist = [
  'Dance learned and rehearsed',
  'Phone upright, steady and fully charged',
  'Light in front, background tidy',
  'Song ready on a speaker',
  'Floor clear, shoes with grip',
  '3-2-1 count, 3 or more takes',
  'No personal details visible',
  'Kids approve the final video',
];
---
<Layout title="Filming tips – Dance Challenge Hub" description="Simple tips for filming dance challenges at home with kids.">
  <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-extrabold sm:text-4xl">Filming tips</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-ink/70">
    Everything you need for a good take at home, from practice to upload.{' '}
    <a href={`${base}/`} class="font-semibold text-pop underline">Pick a challenge</a> first.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2">
    {sections.map((s) => (
      <section class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-ink bg-white p-5 shadow-[4px_4px_0_0_var(--color-ink)]">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold"><span aria-hidden="true">{s.emoji}</span> {s.title}</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-ink/80">
          {s.items.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>

  <section id="checklist" class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border-2 border-ink bg-sun/30 p-5">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">Before you hit record</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {checklist.map((c) => (
        <li>
          <label class="flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer items-center gap-3">
            <input type="checkbox" class="h-5 w-5 accent-pop" />
            <span>{c}</span>
          </label>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>
